{
  "slug": "spiced-cauliflower-and-chickpea-patties",
  "title": "Spiced Cauliflower and Chickpea Patties",
  "blurb": "Golden patties packed with roasted cauliflower, chickpeas and warm curry spices, served in soft buns with cooling yogurt.",
  "steps": [
    "Heat the oven to 200°C. Toss the cauliflower florets with half the olive oil and roast for 20 minutes until tender and lightly golden.",
    "Let the cauliflower cool slightly, then place in a food processor with the chickpeas, green onions, coriander, curry powder, cumin, onion granules, black pepper and salt. Pulse until the mixture comes together but still has some texture.",
    "Transfer to a bowl and stir through the flour and half the breadcrumbs until the mixture binds. Shape into 8 patties and coat each one in the remaining breadcrumbs.",
    "Brush a baking tray with the remaining olive oil and arrange the patties on it. Bake for 25 to 30 minutes, turning halfway, until crisp and golden on both sides.",
    "Split the burger buns and fill each with lettuce, two patties and a spoonful of yogurt."
  ],
